  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Leveraging Partnerships to Tackle Forestry-related Corruption and Crime - Global / Reginal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective is to create significant obstacles to corruption that enables illegal logging and mining in forested areas while undermining conservation policies.
IMPACT: Operational ease of forest crime reduced, mitigating the incentives of such activities thereby contributing to reductions in deforestation.
Outcome 1: Significant obstacles to the corruption that facilitates illegal logging and mining in forested areas that undermines conservation policies
Intermediate Outcome 1: Stakeholders strengthen forestry-related corruption prevention measures and system
Intermediate Outcome 2: Financial crime related to forest corruption cases investigated and prosecuted
Intermediate Outcome 3: Successes are shared among more partners and geographies
Target group: Anti-corruption agencies, law enforcement agencies and other relevant government entities and state-owned enterprises.</narrative>
  </description>
